  "body": "CHECK-045 complete with corrections; QUESTIONABLE/PROJECTION. Owner/predecessor code remained unread and unexecuted. Main conditional danger screens reproduce; installed damage tolerance remains unestablished.\n\nP2: patch cutoffs 54.779991/27.127598 mm; design-hail crushed diameter 80.865106 mm and fluid/Shi/all-energy depths 0.390712/1.675384/5.430417 mm. The 45.890373% pressure reduction requires 2645.660029 kg air at the stated reference; it is not a completed handling plan.\n\nCorrections include the 55 mm growth threshold (19.176311 mm, within the core), Pach units/calibration, printed IEC masses, Perry SF (3.454499160, not 4.095817936), repeated-trial counts and 24 sampled half-kilogram leak times. Nominal P3 SF remains 1.258252477. Original priced witnesses forward-score; stronger local-search witnesses do not rescue the wall/tear fixes. All 56 selected frame comparisons reproduce; all edge classes widen the range and do not establish every-member dynamic cascade. Gross-neutral mass, ground-contact height, valve-control objective and NDI transfer remain explicit qualifications.\n\nOf 1,358 comparisons, 1,287 pass and 71 differ. Eighty-eight exact findings distinguish arithmetic, search, approximation, source and representation issues. Thirty-one NFI rows remain open/nonblocking. All 36 frozen inputs and 46 retrieved-source pins pass; 41 sources are substantive and five access pages quarantined. A later COMMON retry amendment is documented; scientific inputs are unchanged. No time budget. Brief names no successor: stop and file, then SLEEPING.",
